  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Number of local governments with Vulnerability information management system (VIMS) developed and used to identify the vulnerable people 
1.2 No. of municipalities/rural municipalities that conducted Vulnerability assessment using revised indicators to identify vulnerable women in their location
1.3 No. of local governments with policies, guidelines and frameworks related to social protection schemes in place and implemented</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1: 0
1.2: 0
1.3: 0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Develop 2 QR code-based Socio-Economic Vulnerability Information Management Systems to support Local government to allow them to identify vulnerable people/communities for subsequent response to their immediate needs and build access to basic and essential services
2. Conduct socio-economic vulnerability assessment in 2 new project locations in Panchapuri Municipality of Surkhet and Simkot Rural Municipality of Humla in Karnali province
3. Conduct project review and planning workshop</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. 2 QR Code based SEVIMS has been developed and finalized after rounds of consultations with municipal authorities and field testing to incorporate practical needs. The SEVIMS is ready to handover to respective local governments of Beni Municipality and Putalibazaar Municipality in Gandaki Province. 
The municipality has also initiated to collect required data and govt server to host the system live and sustain the initiative. 
2. A detailed socio-economic vulnerability assessment has been conducted and completed by Mid-West University in 2 local government level- Panchapuri Municipality in Surkhet District and Simkot Rural Municipality in Humla district. Total of 980 vulnerable women has been identified in Panchapuri Municipality and 531 in Simikot Rural Municipality. The timely assessment has allowed project to identify actual 1000 beneficiaries to provide support to them. 
3. A 2 days residential workshop was conducted in Chitwan together with representatives of 4 local governments, private sector, 5 NGO partners, 1 govt bank, 2 universities and UNDP team. The workshop reviewed the progress made in 2022 and noted that government and stakeholders have recommended to upscale the project with further commitments and collaboration opportunities by local government.</narrative>
